# Build context for every docker/images/*.Dockerfile is docker/ itself. The
# images COPY exactly the in-container tooling; everything else here runs on the
# host, so the context is an allowlist rather than a denylist.
#
# Only the activate hook and the search-r1 dependency lock are baked. The
# fetch/dataset tooling (autorlbench_fetch.py, autorlbench_dataset.py,
# autorlbench_datasets/) and install-autorlbench-tooling.sh are provisioned at prepare
# time from the repo (see install-autorlbench-tooling.sh), not COPY'd, so they stay
# out of the build context.
#
# search-r1-runtime/ is the exception that has to be in the context: that image
# has no upstream to build FROM, so it installs its stack from the lock the
# recorded runs were produced with (see docker/images/search-r1-verl.Dockerfile).
*
!autorlbench-activate.sh
!verl-moe-token/mcore5047-minimal.patch
!search-r1-runtime/pyproject.toml
!search-r1-runtime/uv.lock
!search-r1-runtime/.python-version
!vl-grpo-recorded-runtime/
!vl-grpo-recorded-runtime/requirements.txt
**/__pycache__
